# Project Report

## Local RAG Document Q&A Chatbot

### 1. Project Title

**Local RAG Document Q&A Chatbot**

---

## 2. Project Overview

The Local RAG Document Q&A Chatbot is a document question-answering system that uses **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)** to answer questions from locally stored PDF documents.

The system combines document processing, semantic search, a local vector database, and a locally running Large Language Model (LLM).

Users can ask questions through a web-based chat interface. The system retrieves relevant information from the ingested documents and provides it as context to the local LLM. The generated response is returned along with source document and page information.

The project was designed to operate locally using **Ollama and Llama 3.2 3B**, without requiring an external LLM API.

---

# 3. Objectives

The main objectives of the project were:

1. Build a fully local document question-answering system.
2. Process PDF documents automatically.
3. Convert document text into meaningful chunks.
4. Generate semantic embeddings for document chunks.
5. Store embeddings in a local vector database.
6. Retrieve relevant document chunks for user questions.
7. Use a local LLM to generate answers based on retrieved context.
8. Prevent unsupported answers when relevant information is unavailable.
9. Provide source document and page references.
10. Expose the system through a FastAPI backend.
11. Provide a simple web-based chatbot interface.
12. Test and document the complete application.

