# 18. Conclusion

The Local RAG Document Q&A Chatbot demonstrates how a local Large Language Model can be combined with document retrieval to create a grounded question-answering system.

The application processes PDF documents, creates semantic embeddings, stores them in ChromaDB, retrieves relevant information for user questions, and provides that information to a locally running Llama 3.2 3B model through Ollama.

The final system provides:

* Local LLM inference
* Semantic document retrieval
* Context-grounded generation
* Source references
* REST API access
* Web-based interaction
* Configurable retrieval
* Logging and testing

The project demonstrates the complete basic workflow of a practical local RAG application, from document ingestion to retrieval and answer generation.
